            <div xml:id="d2">

                <pb facs="0094" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg1"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Peace/2</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 820</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-08-05">August 5, 1935</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your despatch
                    No. 2764 of July 25, 1935, entitled “Possible Inter-American Peace
                    Conference”.</p>
                <p>In general, the information conveyed to you on this subject by the Acting
                    Secretary of Foreign Relations is accurate. The matter is <pb facs="0095" n="2"
                        xml:id="pg2"/> however, still in the formative stage of development and it
                    is, of course, highly desirable that the President’s intentions should not
                    receive any premature publicity. Pending further instructions from the
                    Department, you are requested to make no comment whatever regarding this subject
                    and to treat it as completely and entirely confidential.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner
                            Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
